# Slack domains routed through the selected external VPN tunnel.
#
# Source: Slack Help Center, "Manage Slack connection issues"; Slack uses
# WebSocket over port 443 and calls out wss-primary.slack.com,
# wss-backup.slack.com, and wss-mobile.slack.com for connection testing.
# Slack also recommends checking the workspace-specific URL allowlist at
# https://my.slack.com/help/urls.
#
# dnsmasq's ipset=/domain/... directive matches the listed domain and all
# subdomains, so slack.com covers app/workspace/API/files/WSS hosts under
# *.slack.com. The additional Slack-owned base domains cover common client
# asset, message, file, redirect, and edge/CDN hosts.

# Core app, workspace, API, file, and WebSocket hosts.
slack.com
wss-primary.slack.com
wss-backup.slack.com
wss-mobile.slack.com

# Slack-owned assets, edge/CDN, messages, files, and redirect hosts.
slack-edge.com
slack-files.com
slack-imgs.com
slack-msgs.com
slack-redir.net
slackb.com
